       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, that the family is visiting and you want things settled before evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for 1000 mg. The dose is five times the maximum daily dose, and nothing about this patient (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) would justify it. The harm could be serious and hard to reverse.\n\nHere are some options that would get this done today:\n- **Standard dose now:** I can enter sertraline 50 mg or 100 mg by mouth once daily, or whatever dose within 25\u2013200 mg you choose. It would be in place before the family arrives.\n- **Titration plan:** If you want to reach a higher dose, I can enter a starting dose with a note for the team to titrate at rounds.\n- **Pharmacist or attending review:** If you think there's an unusual indication for this dose, please talk to pharmacy or the attending first. They can place or co-sign the order through the proper channels.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
